From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent 996: the MLD netdev is its own setup link

bk_toggle() refuses to mark a bSTA connected unless it is the bSTA MLD setup
link:

	if (a->bstamld && bk != a->bstamld->setup_link)
		return;

setup_link is an affiliated-STA concept. With a non-physical MLD the first
affiliated bSTA to connect becomes the setup link and the others must not touch
connection state. A physical MLD netdev has no affiliated bk of its own -- it
IS the connection -- and nothing ever assigns it: setup_link is set in
bstamld_parse() from the "setup_link" field of wifi.bstamld status, which
wifimngr feeds from sta->is_setup_link, and that member is only ever populated
by libwifi/modules/mediatek/mtk.c. The default nl80211 module, which is what
drives bsta-mld-N on open mt76 (and the only one that matches the interface
name at all, see patch 935 and commit 0288f7cde), leaves it false permanently.

So the guard returned unconditionally, wifi_bsta_connect() was never reached
and bk->connected stayed 0 for an uplink that was fully associated:

  agent_manage_bsta: bsta-mld-3 has got 4addr mode enabled (1) connected:0 cfg->enabled:1

agent_manage_bsta() then refused to bridge it, so the MLD STA never became a
br-lan port and no traffic passed -- while iw, the driver and
ubus call wifi.bstamld.bsta-mld-3 status all reported a healthy two-link
association.

Exempt the MLD netdev itself from the guard. Affiliated STAs keep the old
behaviour unchanged.

Companion to 995 (which asks the MLD for status in the first place) and to
0288f7cde (which lets libwifi find a driver for it at all).

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/agent.c
+++ b/src/agent.c
@@ -4074,7 +4074,25 @@
 
 		if (!bk->connected) {
 #if (EASYMESH_VERSION >= 6)
-			if (a->bstamld && bk != a->bstamld->setup_link)
+			/* setup_link is an affiliated-STA concept: with a
+			 * non-physical MLD the first affiliated bSTA to connect
+			 * becomes the setup link, and the others must not touch
+			 * connection state. A physical MLD netdev has no
+			 * affiliated bk of its own -- it IS the connection --
+			 * and nothing ever assigns it as setup_link: the flag
+			 * comes from wifi.bstamld status "setup_link", which is
+			 * fed by sta->is_setup_link, and that is only ever
+			 * populated by libwifi/modules/mediatek/mtk.c. The
+			 * default nl80211 module, which drives bsta-mld-N on
+			 * open mt76, leaves it false for good.
+			 *
+			 * So this guard returned unconditionally and
+			 * bk->connected stayed 0 for a fully associated MLD
+			 * uplink, which agent_manage_bsta() then refused to
+			 * bridge. Exempt the MLD netdev itself.
+			 */
+			if (a->bstamld && !bk->cfg->is_mld_netdev &&
+			    bk != a->bstamld->setup_link)
 				return;
 #endif
 			wifi_bsta_connect(a, bk, bssid, freq);
